\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For each integer $m\geq 2$, must a closed connected smooth m-manifold minimally immersed in the unit $S^{m+1}$, with image not totally geodesic, have induced volume at least the least volume among the Clifford hypersurfaces $S^p(\surd (p/m))×S^{m-p}(\surd ((m-p)/m))$, $1\leq p<m$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For each integer $m\geq 2$, must a closed connected smooth m-manifold minimally immersed in the unit $S^{m+1}$, with image not totally geodesic, have induced volume at least the least volume among the Clifford hypersurfaces $S^p(\surd (p/m))×S^{m-p}(\surd ((m-p)/m))$, $1\leq p<m$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Solomon-Yau-least-volume-theorem-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

